---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About 88cutouts — free stickers for Instagram Stories"
  description="88cutouts is a small, free library of transparent PNG stickers, frames and cutouts made for decorating Instagram Stories. No account, no app, no cost."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>About 88cutouts</h1>
      <p>
        88cutouts is a small, hand-kept library of transparent PNG stickers, frames and
        letter cutouts made for one thing: decorating Instagram Stories. Every sticker is
        drawn or assembled for this site, then published as a clean alpha-transparent PNG
        so it drops onto your Story without a white box around it.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is nothing to sign up for. Tap <strong>Copy</strong> on any sticker and it
        goes to your phone's clipboard as an image — then long-press inside the Instagram
        Story editor and paste. If your browser doesn't support copying images,
        <strong>Download</strong> always works as a fallback. One thing worth knowing:
        Instagram <em>feed</em> posts flatten transparency to grey. Stories, DMs and most
        messengers keep it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/ransom-note/">ransom note typewriter</a> works the same way — type a
        message, get a cut-out letter collage back as a transparent PNG.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything here is <strong>free for personal use</strong>: decorate your Stories,
        your group chats, your notes app. Please don't resell the files or bundle them into
        a paid pack. If you want to use something commercially, or you spot an asset that
        shouldn't be here, email me and I'll sort it out.
      </p>
      <p>
        Made by Sarath. Questions, requests, takedowns:
        <a href="mailto:hello@88cutouts.com">hello@88cutouts.com</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
